# Genre Research App environment.
#
# The app runs LOCAL-ONLY with none of these set: capture, the worksheet,
# depth modes, resume, and (later) CSV/Sheets export all work offline.
# These are only needed once the AI broker (build-order step 7) is wired up.

# Supabase. Two uses: (1) accounts (email + password, ANY address — this is not
# Google and does not involve Google); (2) the auth check on the translate Edge
# Function. Project data still stays local in IndexedDB, and feedback still ships
# through the Apps Script sink, so Supabase is the identity layer only.
#
# The anon key is public-safe. Set both to enable the account control in the header
# everywhere; leave blank and the app runs fully local with anonymous feedback.
# Provision with scripts/setup-supabase.sh (needs a Supabase access token), then
# scripts/enable-signup.sh to turn on invite-code signup.
#
# NOTE: the free tier PAUSES a project after 7 days of inactivity, which takes
# sign-in and live translation down with it. Restore it from the dashboard, or via
# POST /v1/projects/<ref>/restore on the Management API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Signup endpoint override. Normally unset: the client derives
# <VITE_SUPABASE_URL>/functions/v1/signup, since the function always lives on the
# same project. Point this at a local `supabase functions serve` to test signup.
VITE_SIGNUP_URL=

# Cost guardrail for the future Claude broker Edge Function (server-side).
# The Claude API key itself lives in the Edge Function, never in this client.
CLAUDE_MONTHLY_SPEND_CAP_USD=50

# Google sign-in (optional). A Google OAuth client id (Web application). With this
# set, the app gains: Sheets export, cross-device cloud sync, and Teams. Leave it
# blank to keep the app fully local/offline with no sign-in UI at all.
#
# Scopes are incremental and requested client-side via GIS:
#   - drive.file  (non-sensitive): sign-in, identity, personal sync, Sheets export.
#   - drive (full, restricted): requested only when creating/joining a team, since
#     a teammate's file is invisible to drive.file. This shows an "unverified app"
#     consent screen until the OAuth app is verified; for an MVP add testers as
#     OAuth "Test users" in the Google Cloud console to bypass it (<100 users).
#
# Authorized JavaScript origins must include the deploy origin (and http://localhost
# for dev). No client secret is used; tokens are obtained in the browser only.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# AI routing via GitHub (optional, automated path). "owner/repo" of a PRIVATE
# repo where captured notes are exchanged with Claude (Max). With this set, the
# AI routing screen can push notes and pull Claude's placements automatically;
# the GitHub token is entered in-app and stored on-device only (never in env).
# Leave blank to use the token-free copy/paste routing path.
VITE_ROUTING_REPO=
VITE_ROUTING_BRANCH=main
